Author: Mazin Fadl <mazen@illumed.net>
Date:   Mon Sep 21 00:25:14 2026 -0400

    em: ex: do not give the external editor a pipe on stdin
    
    External::start() spawned the editor with an explicitly requested stdin
    pipe. We never write to it and never close it, so an editor that reads
    stdin -- or forwards it to a child, as neovide does with neovim -- blocks
    in read() until astroid exits. With neovide this is not even visible as a
    hang: neovim never finishes starting up, so neovide never gets a first
    frame, never creates its window, and the window only appears once astroid
    is terminated and the pipe finally sees EOF.
    
    Leave stdin_pipe_out as nullptr, which makes GLib attach /dev/null to the
    editor's stdin (documented default of g_spawn_async_with_pipes, as well as
    of Glib::spawn_async_with_pipes). Nothing reads the fd afterwards, so the
    now-unused External::stdin member goes away too.

diff --git a/src/modes/editor/external.cc b/src/modes/editor/external.cc
index 6853d4a..6a3ce66 100644
--- a/src/modes/editor/external.cc
+++ b/src/modes/editor/external.cc
@@ -41,7 +41,11 @@ namespace Astroid {
                         Glib::SPAWN_SEARCH_PATH | Glib::SPAWN_DO_NOT_REAP_CHILD,
                         sigc::slot <void> (),
                         &pid,
-                        &stdin,
+                        /* Do not ask for a pipe on the editor's stdin: we never write
+                         * to it, and an editor that reads stdin (or forwards it to a
+                         * child) blocks until astroid exits. Leaving this nullptr makes
+                         * GLib attach /dev/null to the editor's stdin. */
+                        nullptr,
                         &stdout,
                         &stderr
                         );
diff --git a/src/modes/editor/external.hh b/src/modes/editor/external.hh
index 676fcff..fd9c633 100644
--- a/src/modes/editor/external.hh
+++ b/src/modes/editor/external.hh
@@ -29,7 +29,6 @@ namespace Astroid {
       bool editor_started = false;
 
       int pid;
-      int stdin;
       int stdout;
       int stderr;
       refptr<Glib::IOChannel> ch_stdout;
